{
 "_about": "Which downloaded sounds become choices for each game sound (lane B4 part 2). tools/audio/pick_choices.py scores every library.json sound against an entry's rule: +2 per tag in 'tags', +3 per word of 'words' in the title, -10 per word of 'not'; sounds longer than max_s are left out. The best 'count' are cut to max_s, peak-normalised, converted to Ogg in assets/audio/lib/<entry>/ and listed as that sounds.json entry's 'choices', after the synth take ('Made here'). 'default' says which plays until Emerson picks: 'best' (top library match), 'synth' or 'off'. A new entry here (with 'new': {bus, label, ...}) makes a new game sound. 'prefer' (optional): words of the title to make the default when that sound is among the choices. 'pitch' (optional): base pitch for this sound's downloaded choices (below 1 plays lower and longer; for footsteps sized for people). Each choice is levelled to the same average loudness as the synth take it replaces (or the synth take of 'loudness_like', plus 'loudness_db'), peak capped at -1 dBFS, so volume_db keeps its meaning. 'punch': true compresses the take and raises it to a -1 dBFS peak (guns and explosions: more body, as loud as a take can be).",
